## Java 8 and Above

**51. What are the main Java 8 features?** Lambdas, Streams, functional interfaces, Optional, default/static interface methods, method references, `java.time`.

**52. What is a functional interface?** An interface with exactly one abstract method (`Runnable`, `Comparator`, `Predicate`).

**53. `map()` vs `flatMap()`?**
```java
List<List<Integer>> nested = List.of(List.of(1,2), List.of(3));
nested.stream().flatMap(List::stream).toList(); // [1,2,3]
```
`map` is one-to-one; `flatMap` flattens nested streams.

**54. Intermediate vs terminal operations?** Intermediate (lazy, return a Stream): `filter, map, sorted`. Terminal (trigger processing): `collect, forEach, count`.

**55. `findFirst()` vs `findAny()`?** `findAny` is free to return any element (useful for parallel streams).

**56. What is `Optional` and why use it?** A container that may or may not hold a value, reducing `NullPointerException`s.

**57. Find the second-highest number using streams.**
```java
int second = nums.stream().distinct()
    .sorted(Comparator.reverseOrder()).skip(1).findFirst().orElseThrow();
```

**58. Group employees by department and count.**
```java
Map<String, Long> countByDept = emps.stream()
    .collect(Collectors.groupingBy(Emp::getDept, Collectors.counting()));
```

**59. Word frequency count.**
```java
Map<String, Long> freq = Arrays.stream(text.split("\\s+"))
    .collect(Collectors.groupingBy(Function.identity(), Collectors.counting()));
```

**60. What are `record` and `sealed` classes?** `record` is an immutable data carrier with auto-generated members (Java 16). `sealed` restricts which classes can extend/implement a type (Java 17).

**61. What are virtual threads?** Lightweight JVM-managed threads (Java 21) that make high-concurrency blocking code cheap.

