## Coding Problems

**88. Fibonacci**
```java
static int fib(int n) {
    int a = 0, b = 1;
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) { int t = a + b; a = b; b = t; }
    return a;
}
```

**89. Prime check**
```java
static boolean isPrime(int n) {
    if (n < 2) return false;
    for (int i = 2; i * i <= n; i++) if (n % i == 0) return false;
    return true;
}
```

**90. Swap two numbers without a temp**
```java
a = a + b; b = a - b; a = a - b;
```

**91. Find duplicates in an array**
```java
Set<Integer> seen = new HashSet<>();
Set<Integer> dups = new HashSet<>();
for (int n : arr) if (!seen.add(n)) dups.add(n);
```

**92. First non-repeating character**
```java
Map<Character, Integer> m = new LinkedHashMap<>();
for (char c : s.toCharArray()) m.merge(c, 1, Integer::sum);
for (var e : m.entrySet()) if (e.getValue() == 1) { System.out.println(e.getKey()); break; }
```

**93. Check anagram**
```java
char[] a = s1.toCharArray(), b = s2.toCharArray();
Arrays.sort(a); Arrays.sort(b);
boolean anagram = Arrays.equals(a, b);
```

**94. Binary search**
```java
static int search(int[] arr, int key) {
    int lo = 0, hi = arr.length - 1;
    while (lo <= hi) {
        int mid = lo + (hi - lo) / 2;
        if (arr[mid] == key) return mid;
        else if (arr[mid] < key) lo = mid + 1;
        else hi = mid - 1;
    }
    return -1;
}
```

**95. Reverse a linked list**
```java
Node prev = null, cur = head;
while (cur != null) {
    Node next = cur.next;
    cur.next = prev;
    prev = cur;
    cur = next;
}
head = prev;
```

**96. Armstrong number**
```java
int sum = 0, t = n;
while (t > 0) { int d = t % 10; sum += d * d * d; t /= 10; }
boolean isArmstrong = (sum == n);   // for 3-digit numbers
```

**97. Thread-safe Singleton (enum)**
```java
public enum Singleton { INSTANCE }
```

**98. Two-sum using HashMap**
```java
Map<Integer,Integer> map = new HashMap<>();
for (int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
    int need = target - nums[i];
    if (map.containsKey(need)) return new int[]{map.get(need), i};
    map.put(nums[i], i);
}
```

**99. Producer-Consumer with BlockingQueue**
```java
BlockingQueue<Integer> q = new ArrayBlockingQueue<>(5);
Thread producer = new Thread(() -> { try { for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) q.put(i); } catch (InterruptedException e) {} });
Thread consumer = new Thread(() -> { try { while (true) System.out.println(q.take()); } catch (InterruptedException e) {} });
producer.start(); consumer.start();
```

